{"code":"sv-SE","name":"Swedish","native":"Svenska","badge":"SV","tts":"sv-SE","sheets":[{"id":"C1","mode":"utility","kind":"core","title":"Keep it alive","blurb":"The lines that rescue any conversation. You’ll use these every day, everywhere.","items":[{"id":"c1.1","t":"Jag förstår inte.","say":"yah fur-STOHR IN-teh","en":"I don't understand.","ctx":["work","travel","chat"]},{"id":"c1.2","t":"Jag vet inte.","say":"yah veet IN-teh","en":"I don't know.","ctx":["work","travel","chat"]},{"id":"c1.3","t":"Ett ögonblick, tack.","say":"et UR-gon-blik, tak","en":"One moment, please.","ctx":["work","shops","phone"],"tags":"wait hold on sec moment"},{"id":"c1.4","t":"Kan du säga det igen?","say":"kan doo SEH-ya deh ee-YEN","en":"Can you say that again?","ctx":["work","travel","chat"],"tags":"repeat again pardon what"},{"id":"c1.5","t":"Lite långsammare, tack.","say":"LEE-teh LONG-sam-ma-reh, tak","en":"Slower, please.","ctx":["travel","chat"],"tags":"slow slowly speak"},{"id":"c1.6","t":"Vad heter ”…” på svenska?","say":"vah HEE-ter … poh SVEN-ska","en":"What’s “…” in Swedish?","ctx":["everywhere"],"tags":"word translate"}]},{"id":"C2","mode":"utility","kind":"core","title":"React like you belong","blurb":"Short reactions that make you sound fluent while you listen.","items":[{"id":"c2.1","t":"Visst.","say":"vist","en":"Sure. / Of course.","ctx":["work","shops","chat"],"tags":"yes ok okay sure course"},{"id":"c2.2","t":"Precis.","say":"preh-SEES","en":"Exactly. / Right.","ctx":["work","chat"],"tags":"yes right correct agree"},{"id":"c2.3","t":"Jag tror det.","say":"yah troor deh","en":"I think so.","ctx":["work","chat"]},{"id":"c2.4","t":"Verkligen?","say":"VERK-lee-gen","en":"Really?","ctx":["chat"]},{"id":"c2.5","t":"Inga problem.","say":"ING-a proo-BLEM","en":"No problem. / No worries.","ctx":["work","travel","chat"],"tags":"welcome fine ok"},{"id":"c2.6","t":"Vad kul!","say":"vah KOOL","en":"Great! / How nice!","ctx":["chat","family"],"tags":"cool awesome nice"}]},{"id":"C3","mode":"utility","kind":"core","title":"Frames","blurb":"Phrases with a blank. Drop in any word you know and you have a new sentence.","items":[{"id":"c3.1","t":"Var är {x}?","say":"var air {x}","en":"Where is {x}?","ctx":["travel","toilets"],"tags":"where find","frame":true,"takes":"noun","ex":"bathroom","fits":["place","work"]},{"id":"c3.2","t":"Jag skulle vilja ha {x}.","say":"yah SKOO-leh VIL-ya hah {x}","en":"I'd like {x}.","ctx":["food","shops"],"tags":"want like would order get","frame":true,"takes":"noun","ex":"coffee","fits":["thing"]},{"id":"c3.3","t":"Har ni {x}?","say":"har nee {x}","en":"Do you have {x}?","ctx":["shops","food"],"tags":"have any got there","frame":true,"takes":"noun","ex":"water","fits":["thing"]},{"id":"c3.4","t":"{x}, tack.","say":"{x}, tak","en":"{x}, please.","ctx":["everywhere"],"tags":"please give","frame":true,"takes":"noun","ex":"bill","fits":["thing","work"]},{"id":"c3.5","t":"Jag måste {x}.","say":"yah MOS-teh {x}","en":"I have to {x}.","ctx":["work","plans"],"tags":"must need got","frame":true,"takes":"verb","ex":"leave"},{"id":"c3.6","t":"Får jag {x}?","say":"fohr yah {x}","en":"Can I {x}?","ctx":["work","travel"],"tags":"can may could allowed","frame":true,"takes":"verb","ex":"comein"}]},{"id":"W","mode":"utility","kind":"lens","lens":"work","title":"Work: Slack & meetings","blurb":"Mostly lines you already know, plus two new ones and some words for your blanks.","items":[{"id":"w.1","t":"Jag kollar.","say":"yah KOL-lar","en":"I’ll check.","tags":"look into get back"},{"id":"w.2","t":"Jag har ett möte.","say":"yah har et MUR-teh","en":"I have a meeting.","tags":"busy call"}],"core":["c1.3","c1.1","c1.2","c1.4","c2.1","c2.2"],"words":["meeting","file","screen","message","tomorrow"]},{"id":"T1","mode":"utility","kind":"lens","lens":"travel","title":"Travel: Eating out","blurb":"Your frames do most of the ordering. A few new lines and some food words.","diet":true,"items":[{"id":"t1.1","t":"Är det starkt?","say":"air deh starkt","en":"Is it spicy?","tags":"hot chili"},{"id":"t1.2","t":"Utan lök, tack.","say":"OO-tan lurk, tak","en":"Without onion, please."},{"id":"t1.3","t":"Vad rekommenderar du?","say":"vah reh-ko-men-DEH-rar doo","en":"What do you recommend?"},{"id":"t1.4","t":"Jag äter inte kött.","say":"yah EH-ter IN-teh shurt","en":"I don't eat meat.","tags":"vegetarian vegan meat"}],"core":["c3.2","c3.4","c3.3","c1.1"],"words":["water","coffee","bill","menu","beer","this"]},{"id":"T2","mode":"utility","kind":"lens","lens":"travel","title":"Travel: Shopping & money","blurb":"Want, have, one moment: all core. Four new lines.","items":[{"id":"t2.1","t":"Vad kostar det?","say":"vah KOS-tar deh","en":"How much is it?","tags":"price cost how much"},{"id":"t2.2","t":"Jag tittar bara.","say":"yah TIT-tar BAH-ra","en":"I'm just looking."},{"id":"t2.3","t":"Jag tar den.","say":"yah tar den","en":"I'll take it."},{"id":"t2.4","t":"Kan jag betala med kort?","say":"kan yah beh-TAH-la meh koort","en":"Can I pay by card?","tags":"credit card cash pay"}],"core":["c3.2","c3.3","c1.3"],"words":["this","bag"]},{"id":"T3","mode":"utility","kind":"lens","lens":"travel","title":"Travel: Getting around","blurb":"Ask with your core frame, then understand the answer.","items":[{"id":"t3.1","t":"Är det långt?","say":"air deh longt","en":"Is it far?"},{"id":"t3.2","t":"Till flygplatsen, tack.","say":"til FLEEG-plat-sen, tak","en":"To the airport, please. (taxi)","tags":"taxi cab driver"},{"id":"t3.3","t":"vänster · höger · rakt fram","say":"VEN-ster · HUR-ger · rakt fram","en":"left · right · straight on","hear":true,"tags":"directions"}],"core":["c3.1","c1.5","c1.4"],"words":["station","airport","hotel"]},{"id":"T4","mode":"utility","kind":"lens","lens":"travel","title":"Travel: Toilets, help & signs","blurb":"Ask with your core frame. New: a few emergency lines and the signs you’ll see.","signs":true,"items":[{"id":"t4.1","t":"Hjälp!","say":"yelp","en":"Help!","tags":"emergency"},{"id":"t4.2","t":"Det finns inget toalettpapper.","say":"deh fins ING-et too-a-LET-pap-per","en":"There's no toilet paper."},{"id":"t4.3","t":"Jag mår illa.","say":"yah mohr IL-la","en":"I feel sick.","tags":"ill unwell doctor"},{"id":"t4.4","t":"Ring efter en ambulans!","say":"ring EF-ter en am-boo-LANS","en":"Please call an ambulance.","tags":"emergency doctor"}],"core":["c3.1","c3.4","c1.1"],"words":["bathroom","pharmacy","hospital"]},{"id":"F","mode":"utility","kind":"lens","lens":"family","title":"Family & small talk","blurb":"Reactions carry the conversation. Four new lines to start one.","items":[{"id":"f.1","t":"Trevligt att träffas.","say":"TREEV-likt at TREF-fas","en":"Nice to meet you."},{"id":"f.2","t":"Var kommer du ifrån?","say":"var KOM-mer doo ee-FROHN","en":"Where are you from?"},{"id":"f.3","t":"Vad jobbar du med?","say":"vah YOB-bar doo meh","en":"What do you do (for work)?"},{"id":"f.4","t":"Det är jättegott!","say":"deh air YET-teh-got","en":"It's delicious!"}],"core":["c2.1","c2.4","c2.6","c2.3"]},{"id":"B1","mode":"basic","kind":"basic","title":"Hello & basics","blurb":"Greetings, yes and no, please and thanks.","items":[{"id":"b1.1","t":"Hej.","say":"hay","en":"Hello.","tags":"hi hey"},{"id":"b1.2","t":"God morgon.","say":"goo MOR-ron","en":"Good morning."},{"id":"b1.3","t":"Hur mår du?","say":"hoor mohr doo","en":"How are you?"},{"id":"b1.4","t":"Ja. · Nej.","say":"yah · nay","en":"Yes. · No."},{"id":"b1.5","t":"Tack.","say":"tak","en":"Please. / Thanks. (tack does both)"},{"id":"b1.6","t":"Tack så mycket.","say":"tak soh MUY-keh","en":"Thank you very much."},{"id":"b1.7","t":"Förlåt.","say":"fur-LOHT","en":"Sorry. / Excuse me.","tags":"excuse me pardon apologize"},{"id":"b1.8","t":"Hej då.","say":"hay doh","en":"Goodbye.","tags":"bye"}]},{"id":"B2","mode":"basic","kind":"basic","title":"Numbers","blurb":"Enough for prices, times and phone numbers.","items":[{"id":"b2.1","t":"ett · två · tre","say":"et · tvoh · treh","en":"1 · 2 · 3"},{"id":"b2.2","t":"fyra · fem · sex","say":"FEE-ra · fem · seks","en":"4 · 5 · 6"},{"id":"b2.3","t":"sju · åtta · nio","say":"shoo · OT-ta · NEE-oo","en":"7 · 8 · 9"},{"id":"b2.4","t":"tio · tjugo · hundra","say":"TEE-oo · SHOO-go · HUN-dra","en":"10 · 20 · 100"}]},{"id":"B3","mode":"basic","kind":"blueprint","title":"Blueprint","blurb":"How the language works, on one page. Spot the pattern; skip the rulebook.","items":[{"id":"b3.1","t":"Äpplet är rött.","say":"EP-let air rurt","en":"The apple is red.","note":"“the” is a suffix: äpple → äpplet"},{"id":"b3.2","t":"Jag äter äpplet.","say":"yah EH-ter EP-let","en":"I eat the apple.","note":"verb second · the same form for every person"},{"id":"b3.3","t":"Jag åt äpplet.","say":"yah oht EP-let","en":"I ate the apple.","note":"past changes the vowel: äter → åt"},{"id":"b3.4","t":"Jag vill äta äpplet.","say":"yah vil EH-ta EP-let","en":"I want to eat the apple.","note":"helper + infinitive"},{"id":"b3.5","t":"Äter du äpplen?","say":"EH-ter doo EP-len","en":"Do you eat apples?","note":"verb first = question"}]}],"words":[{"id":"bathroom","t":"toaletten","say":"too-a-LET-ten","en":"the bathroom","kind":"noun","cat":"place","tags":"toilet restroom washroom wc loo"},{"id":"pharmacy","t":"apoteket","say":"a-poo-TEE-ket","en":"the pharmacy","kind":"noun","cat":"place","tags":"drugstore chemist medicine"},{"id":"hospital","t":"sjukhuset","say":"SHOOK-hoo-set","en":"the hospital","kind":"noun","cat":"place","tags":"doctor emergency"},{"id":"station","t":"stationen","say":"sta-SHOO-nen","en":"the station","kind":"noun","cat":"place","tags":"train metro subway"},{"id":"airport","t":"flygplatsen","say":"FLEEG-plat-sen","en":"the airport","kind":"noun","cat":"place","tags":"flight plane"},{"id":"hotel","t":"hotellet","say":"hoo-TEL-let","en":"the hotel","kind":"noun","cat":"place","tags":"room stay"},{"id":"water","t":"vatten","say":"VAT-ten","en":"water","kind":"noun","cat":"thing","tags":"drink"},{"id":"coffee","t":"en kaffe","say":"en KAF-feh","en":"a coffee","kind":"noun","cat":"thing","tags":"cafe drink"},{"id":"bill","t":"notan","say":"NOO-tan","en":"the bill","kind":"noun","cat":"thing","tags":"check pay receipt"},{"id":"menu","t":"menyn","say":"meh-NEEN","en":"the menu","kind":"noun","cat":"thing","tags":"food order"},{"id":"beer","t":"en öl","say":"en url","en":"a beer","kind":"noun","cat":"thing","tags":"drink alcohol"},{"id":"this","t":"den här","say":"den hair","en":"this one","kind":"noun","cat":"thing","tags":"that one"},{"id":"bag","t":"en påse","say":"en POH-seh","en":"a bag","kind":"noun","cat":"thing","tags":"plastic bag"},{"id":"meeting","t":"mötet","say":"MUR-tet","en":"the meeting","kind":"noun","cat":"work","tags":"call standup zoom"},{"id":"file","t":"filen","say":"FEE-len","en":"the file","kind":"noun","cat":"work","tags":"document doc"},{"id":"screen","t":"skärmen","say":"SHAR-men","en":"the screen","kind":"noun","cat":"work","tags":"share screen"},{"id":"message","t":"meddelandet","say":"MED-deh-lan-det","en":"the message","kind":"noun","cat":"work","tags":"slack text dm"},{"id":"tomorrow","t":"i morgon","say":"ee MOR-ron","en":"tomorrow","kind":"time"},{"id":"leave","t":"gå","say":"goh","en":"go","kind":"verb","tags":"leave go"},{"id":"comein","t":"komma in","say":"KOM-ma in","en":"come in","kind":"verb","tags":"enter"},{"id":"pay","t":"betala","say":"beh-TAH-la","en":"pay","kind":"verb","tags":"card cash"}],"diet":{"title":"Allergi · läs gärna","ask":"Innehåller rätten något av detta?","askEn":"Does this dish contain any of these?","thanks":"Tack så mycket!","note":"","options":{"peanut":{"label":"Peanut allergy","t":"Jag har en svår jordnötsallergi. Jag kan inte äta jordnötter eller jordnötsolja.","en":"I have a severe peanut allergy. I can't eat peanuts or peanut oil."},"shellfish":{"label":"Shellfish allergy","t":"Jag har en svår allergi mot skaldjur (räkor, krabba, musslor).","en":"I have a severe shellfish allergy (shrimp, crab, shellfish)."},"gluten":{"label":"No gluten","t":"Jag kan inte äta gluten (vete, korn, råg).","en":"I can't eat gluten (wheat)."},"vegetarian":{"label":"No meat or fish","t":"Jag äter inte kött, kyckling eller fisk.","en":"I don't eat meat, chicken or fish."},"pork":{"label":"No pork","t":"Jag äter inte fläsk.","en":"I don't eat pork."}}},"signs":[{"t":"TOALETT · WC","en":"Restroom"},{"t":"DAMER · HERRAR","en":"Women · Men"},{"t":"UTGÅNG · INGÅNG","en":"Exit · Entrance"},{"t":"TRYCK · DRAG","en":"Push · Pull"},{"t":"NÖDUTGÅNG","en":"Emergency exit"}]}